== drift — issue #141. One revision, two windows. Not a gate. ==

base: df999da (HEAD)
new:  df999da (working tree)
Preparing worktree (detached HEAD df999da)
built two linux/amd64 bench binaries (static)
methodology: -count=30 -benchtime=1s, GOMAXPROCS=1, filter=BenchmarkKernel|BenchmarkPeak
        benchstat compares the two logs, ignoring keel-bench-clock-mhz,keel-bench-flops — configuration
        keys that describe the run rather than the build, and which forked the table
        into two delta-free halves when they were not ignored (#50, T20).
        both arms are the same source, so any delta below is the host between two
        windows, not the code: a null A/B whose expected reading is a wash.
        read the absolute sec/op and GFLOP/s columns, not only the delta -- the ratio
        the gate publishes divides two terms a host effect moves together.

